course: dictionary
lesson: 11896
title: Brotherhood
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Brotherhood is a noun. Its simplest meaning is the feeling of friendship and loyalty between people, like the feeling between brothers. «The team showed a real sense of brotherhood when they helped each other up after a fall.» Here the word shows how the players stood by one another.
explain: Brotherhood can also mean a group of people who share the same aims or job. «The monks in the old abbey belong to a religious brotherhood.» The clue is the word religious, which tells you the group shares beliefs. The monks are not all brothers by birth, so this meaning is about a shared purpose.
explain: Brotherhood can also mean the relationship of being brothers. Use the other words in the sentence to choose the right meaning. If the sentence is about a group, it is meaning 2. If it is about two people related as brothers, it is meaning 3.
fact: Brotherhood is a noun, and it is usually uncountable: you say brotherhood, not a brotherhood, when you mean the feeling.
fact: «Brotherhood» means friendship and loyalty between people, like the feeling between brothers.
fact: «A brotherhood» can mean a group or society of people with the same aims or job, such as a religious brotherhood.
fact: Phrases to learn: «a sense of brotherhood», «the brotherhood of all people», «a religious brotherhood».
fact: When you meet a word with more than one meaning, read the whole sentence and ask which meaning fits best.
exercise: «The monks in the old abbey belong to a religious brotherhood.» What does brotherhood mean here? | A type of weather | A tall stone tower | *A group of people with the same aims, such as monks | A kind of bread
exercise: «The team showed a true sense of brotherhood, helping each other every day.» What does brotherhood mean here? | *Friendship and loyalty between people | Rules about football | A hot drink | Being very tired after training
exercise: Ella says brotherhood only means being real brothers. Which meaning is wider? | Being a brother in a shop | *Friendship and loyalty between people, like the feeling between brothers, and a group with shared aims | Friendship and loyalty between people, like the feeling between brothers | A brown wooden table
test: What does the phrase «the brotherhood of all people» suggest? | Digging holes in the garden | *Fairness and peace between all people | Fast cars and loud music | Counting coins in a box
test: Which word means the relationship of being brothers? | Kindness | *Brotherhood | Castle | Harvest
exam: «The brotherhood of the village rebuilt the bridge after the flood.» What does brotherhood mean here? | Being the oldest brother in the family | *A group of people working together for a shared aim | A kind of village bread | The feeling of being cold and wet
